#Your program should take an even length string as input which length was greater than or equals to 6. 
#Display the output by combining the last character from the first half and first character from the second half of the string.  
# In case of string is not even length and the number of characters  less than 6 , you can display  output as “INVALID INPUT STRING”

     #Example: #input:   MOTHER   
                    #output:   TH
x=input("enter a string:")
if len(x)%2 ==0 and len(x)>=6:
    first = x[0:len(x)//2]
    last =x[len(x) // 2:len(x)]
    output = first[len(first)-1]+last[0]
    print(output)
else:
   print(" in valid input")
